<BaseLayout
  title="Free Real Estate Calculators | 16 Online Tools"
  description="Explore 16 free real estate calculators for mortgages, affordability, rental returns, commissions and selling costs. Clear estimates, no signup required."
  canonical="https://everyrealestatecalculator.com/tools/"
  extraStyles={["../assets/tools.css","../assets/tool-listing.css"]}
  extraScripts={["../assets/tool-registry.js","../assets/tool-search.js","../assets/tool-directory.js"]}
>
<main id="main"><section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap tools-intro"><div class="tools-intro-copy"><h1>Free Real Estate Calculators</h1><p>Explore 16 free real estate calculators for buying, investing and selling. Compare estimates, understand the assumptions, and plan your next step.</p></div><div class="trust-chips" aria-label="Calculator benefits"><span>✓ No signup</span><span>✓ Free to use</span><span>✓ Calculations stay in your browser</span></div></div></section><section class="section listing-section"><div class="wrap"><h2 class="visually-hidden">Available tools</h2><div class="listing-panel"><div class="listing-search-wrap"><svg class="listing-search-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="m16 16 4.5 4.5"/></svg><input id="tool-search" class="listing-search" type="search" placeholder="Search tools by name or purpose… e.g. mortgage, cap rate, tax" aria-label="Search tools"></div><div class="listing-meta"><div id="tool-filters" role="group" aria-label="Tool categories"></div><p id="tool-count" class="listing-count" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p></div></div><div id="tool-grid" class="tool-listing-grid"></div><div class="no-results" id="no-results"></div><noscript><p class="note">Enable JavaScript to search and filter the directory. Every calculator is also listed with a description below.</p></noscript><div class="listing-banner"><div><p class="listing-banner-title">Managing clients after the numbers?</p><p class="listing-banner-sub">Turn a calculation into a follow-up in RealtorCRM.</p></div><a class="btn btn-primary" href="../real-estate-crm/">See RealtorCRM →</a></div></div></section><section class="section tools-directory"><div class="wrap"><details class="directory-details"><summary class="directory-summary"><span>Browse plain-text directory of all 16 calculators</span><span class="directory-summary-hint" aria-hidden="true">Show list</span></summary><div class="directory-details-body"><h2>All sixteen calculators, in plain language</h2><p class="directory-intro">Every calculator below runs free in your browser, shows its formula or method, and includes a worked example you can check by hand. Use the search and filters above for the card view, or browse the full list here.</p><h3>Buying</h3><ul class="directory-list"><li><a href="mortgage-calculator/">Mortgage Calculator</a><p>Work out the full monthly payment on a home loan: principal and interest, plus property tax, homeowners insurance, HOA dues and PMI for the costs you enter. For buyers and owners comparing loan terms — the total payment matters more than the loan payment alone.</p></li><li><a href="down-payment-calculator/">Down Payment Calculator</a><p>Work out the down payment at 3%, 3.5%, 5%, 10%, 15% and 20%, the closing costs on top of it, and the total cash to close — with the monthly payment and PMI priced for every tier. For buyers planning how much cash a purchase really takes.</p></li><li><a href="home-affordability-calculator/">Home Affordability Calculator</a><p>Start from the monthly payment you can carry and solve backwards to a top home price, using your income, debts and down payment. For buyers who want a budget before they start shopping.</p></li><li><a href="rent-vs-buy-calculator/">Rent vs Buy Calculator</a><p>Compare the full multi-year cost of renting against buying, including equity, selling costs and the year buying pulls ahead. For anyone deciding whether a move is worth it yet — or at all.</p></li></ul><h3>Investing</h3><ul class="directory-list"><li><a href="cap-rate-calculator/">Cap Rate Calculator</a><p>Compare a rental property's net operating income with its price or value as a percentage — its income yield before financing. For investors screening deals; because it ignores the mortgage, it compares properties rather than loans.</p></li><li><a href="rental-yield-calculator/">Rental Yield Calculator</a><p>Turn a property’s price and rent into its gross and net yield — the rent as a percentage of the price, before and after vacancy and running costs. For investors screening rentals quickly, and for the rent a property must achieve to hit a target yield.</p></li><li><a href="commercial-real-estate-calculator/">Commercial Real Estate Calculator</a><p>Underwrite a commercial purchase the way a lender does: NOI and cap rate on the property, DSCR and cash-on-cash on the deal, and the balloon balance due when the loan term ends. For buyers of shops, offices, warehouses and small apartment blocks.</p></li><li><a href="irr-calculator/">IRR Calculator</a><p>Follow a rental deal year by year — cash flow, growing rent, the loan paying down and the final sale — and solve it into one annualized return. For investors judging a whole hold, not just the first year.</p></li><li><a href="wholesale-calculator/">Wholesale Calculator</a><p>Work backwards from a property's after repair value to the most you can offer the seller — the investor discount, repairs, closing costs and your wholesale fee, on the 70% rule. For wholesalers pricing a deal every party can still profit from.</p></li><li><a href="noi-calculator/">NOI Calculator</a><p>Add up a property's effective rental income and subtract its operating expenses — never the mortgage — to get net operating income per year and per month. The figure behind cap rate, income-based valuations and lender reviews.</p></li><li><a href="property-investment-calculator/">Property Investment Calculator</a><p>Model one rental end to end: monthly cash flow, cash-on-cash return, cap rate, DSCR and the rent at which the deal breaks even. For landlords checking whether a specific property actually pays.</p></li><li><a href="roi-calculator/">ROI Calculator</a><p>Project a rental's whole-hold return — cash flow plus appreciation plus loan paydown — as a total percentage and an annualized rate. For investors comparing holding a property against selling it or choosing a different deal.</p></li></ul><h3>Selling</h3><ul class="directory-list"><li><a href="bridge-loan-calculator/">Bridge Loan Calculator</a><p>Estimate how much you can borrow against your current home to buy the next one first, the interest-only cost while the two homes overlap, and the cash left after your sale settles. For movers who need to buy before they sell.</p></li></ul><h3>Tax</h3><ul class="directory-list"><li><a href="capital-gains-tax-calculator/">Capital Gains Tax Calculator</a><p>Estimate the federal tax on selling a property: the gain, the primary-residence exclusion, depreciation recapture and your net proceeds after tax. For sellers and investors planning a sale — an estimate to plan with, not a tax filing.</p></li><li><a href="depreciation-calculator/">Depreciation Calculator</a><p>Work out the yearly tax depreciation on a rental property: the depreciable basis after the land comes out, the part first year under the mid-month convention, and the full 27.5 or 39-year schedule to the final year. For landlords and investors claiming the deduction properly.</p></li></ul><h3>For agents</h3><ul class="directory-list"><li><a href="commission-calculator/">Commission Calculator</a><p>Turn a sale price and commission rate into the amount that actually reaches the agent after the brokerage split and transaction fees, with the seller's total commission cost shown too. For agents forecasting income and sellers checking what a sale costs.</p></li></ul></div></details></div></section></main>
</BaseLayout>
